  "review": {
    "description": "Quadratic predecessor-certificate proof simplification and independent validation.",
    "assessment": "No proof, public API or data defect found. Splitting the natural input into zero and successor cases and simplifying multiplication by zero leaves linear facts discharged by omega. Both target builds, two direct clients, focused check, old axiom reports and corrected boundary probes pass with matching logs and no warnings. Original snapshot matches the parent commit; final snapshot matches the source commit. All 12 recorded phase statuses and source/log/object hashes were checked.",
    "graph": "All 77 current source hashes and parsed project-import edges match the corrected graph receipt. The focus check\u2019s previously omitted edge to QuadraticTreeCodeGraphs was corrected after independent review; that target was already an explicit root.",
    "prerequisites": "All 22 prior prebuild records and four borrowed DAG source/object hashes were verified, with the original target snapshot used to authenticate its earlier prebuild.",
    "failed_probes": "Both initial proof prototypes failed and their error logs are retained; their temporary source was overwritten. Two boundary-check drafts also failed and their exact sources, logs and status records are retained; the corrected boundary retry passed."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "AnnotatedProofChecker, ComposeRepresentation, ObjectOmegaSemiring and QuarticCompiler sources have newer timestamps than resolved cached objects; timestamps alone do not establish incompatibility. Earlier project and external dependencies remain precompiled.",
    "The earlier proof-probe sources were overwritten and their standalone success/failure statuses were not separately captured in JSON; failure logs include nonzero-exit diagnostics and the successful probe log contains timing.",
    "The initial boundary failures are excluded from the passing comparison; baseline-records.json includes the separately recorded corrected retry.",
    "Compiled objects and overlay symlinks are excluded; hashes and prior receipts are retained."
  ]
